    "problem_statement": "A task blocked in sem_wait on one semaphore receives a signal whose handler itself successfully takes a second semaphore. After the handler returns, the originally blocked sem_wait must resume and return -EINTR, but on the buggy kernel it instead returns success (OK). The signal-handler test exercises this: the waiter task blocks on sem1, a second semaphore is taken inside the signal handler, and the test asserts the waiter's sem_wait resumes with -EINTR; on the buggy kernel it reports an 'awakened with no error' error when the waiter returns OK.",
